     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Any way to turn off reactive function return value caching?  (for memory management purposes)</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "AMBgTNUHBwAJ",
   "from": "Joe Cheng",
   "author": "ca443e6eaa0e78ed",
   "date": "2016-09-05T15:47:56Z",
   "subject": "Re: how to turn off reactive() return value caching",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Yes, just convert it to a zero argument function. <br><br>r &lt;- reactive({...})<br><br>Becomes<br><br>r &lt;- function() {...}<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
